Z||000009||AusFiero||03-15-2001||11:06 PM||||I have a Canadian Fiero. 86 GT with T-tops.<BR>Bought it off the original Canadian owner who bought it to Australia with her when she emmigrated here.<P>I wish we could buy Fieros in Australia for the figures you's guys umm and ah about.<P>My car owes me $30,000 AUS. Insurance company just valued it at $25,000 this renewal. <P>There is cheaper Fieros out here but you get what you pay for. Mine was rundown when I bought it and $16,000 of the above 30 k was spent on parts.<P>Granted the new 3rd world value Australian dollar (49c US) doesn't help any but I bought the car when our dollar was worth more than a peso. Replacement value to bring another over is now ridiculously high.<P>But its worth every cent in my books (c:||||reg||1
Z||000010||William Federle||03-16-2001||08:50 PM||||I think that that car with the leather seats and good paint job and low miles sounds like its well worth the money. I got mine for $500.00 US but the paint was all faded, the left hand seat is in very poor condition, it's a 4 cyl with about 180K miles on it, the sun roof leaks and it burns oil until it warms up. Also I had to replace the entire cooling system and the suspension is shot. <P>So I think you got your money's worth if the suspension is OK.||||reg||1
